ions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/chriskonopka/consuming-app/commit/33b67cf939dfec5534adadc0a9bb9de24f943fd3","node_id":"C_kwDOSW_WwdoAKDMzYjY3Y2Y5MzlkZmVjNTUzNGFkYWRjMGE5YmI5ZGUyNGY5NDNmZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chriskonopka/consuming-app/commit/58aa96adfa2cbf76e7dc337d3b2ac580bfd4d4c2","sha":"58aa96adfa2cbf76e7dc337d3b2ac580bfd4d4c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chriskonopka/consuming-app/commits/58aa96adfa2cbf76e7dc337d3b2ac580bfd4d4c2"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/chriskonopka/consuming-app/commit/b4cb5432f336239c6ac3b8747d32d8d0032c7887","sha":"b4cb5432f336239c6ac3b8747d32d8d0032c7887","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chriskonopka/consuming-app/commits/b4cb5432f336239c6ac3b8747d32d8d0032c7887"}],"sha":"33b67cf939dfec5534adadc0a9bb9de24f943fd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chriskonopka/consuming-app/commits/33b67cf939dfec5534adadc0a9bb9de24f943fd3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4922472?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chrisgoddard","id":4922472,"login":"chrisgoddard","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MjI0NzI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chriskonopka/consuming-app/commits/b4cb5432f336239c6ac3b8747d32d8d0032c7887/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T08:01:29Z","email":"chris@Christophers-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Christopher Konopka"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T08:01:29Z","email":"chris@Christophers-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Christopher Konopka"},"message":"feat(viewer): image rendering — revive slice 5 (image-only scope)\n\nSurgical cherry-pick of the image-rendering pieces from the unmerged\nslice-5 commit `ded011d` onto current main. The Office/text \"Preview not\navailable\" fallback was deliberately reverted earlier when we realised\nthe API converts docx/xlsx/html/txt/md/rtf to PDF on the fly — those\nformats already render through the existing PDF path. Images were the\ngenuine gap; this PR closes it.\n\nWhat lands:\n\n* `ImageRenderer.tsx` — `<img>` blob-URL pattern + reused\n  `<HighlightOverlay>` via a synthetic `OverlayViewport` (scale 1, image\n  natural dimensions) so the drift guard runs identically on PDFs and\n  images.\n* `useImageDocument.ts` — auth-aware image fetch via `useApiClient.raw()`,\n  ReadableStream → Blob → object URL through `bytesToBlobUrl`. Revokes\n  the URL on documentId change / unmount.\n* `bytesToBlobUrl.ts` — stream branch implementation (was scaffold).\n* `renderStrategyFor()` in `shared/types/viewer.ts` — content-type\n  classifier (`pdf` | `image` | `unsupported`). DocumentViewer routes\n  `image` → ImageRenderer and `pdf` / `unsupported` → existing pdf.js\n  path. The defensive `unsupported` branch is reachable only if the API\n  returns an unexpected content-type — real Office/text documents come\n  back as application/pdf after server-side conversion.\n* `DocumentViewer.tsx` — content-type branch + page-nav hidden for\n  non-PDFs + PageUp/Down gated on `isPdf`. Preserves the recent\n  `fitToWidthPx` clamp and the 404 \"not longer available\" banner.\n* `HighlightOverlay.tsx` — `OverlayViewport` interface replaces direct\n  `PageViewport` import (structural subset; same shape used by both\n  sides).\n* `setupTests.ts` — counter-based `URL.createObjectURL` /\n  `revokeObjectURL` jsdom shims for the image tests.\n* Sample PNG fixture for tests.\n\nWhat''s deliberately NOT included (also in `ded011d`, but out of scope):\n\n* `UnsupportedDocumentFallback.*` — wrong premise (API converts non-image\n  non-PDF to PDF).\n* `AppShell.module.scss` / `Panel.module.scss` responsive breakpoints —\n  separate concern, future slice.\n* `IndexerHost.tsx` shared-collection read-only telemetry — separate\n  concern, future slice.\n* Slice-5 e2e specs — all responsive-layout, no image-rendering coverage;\n  unit-level coverage (ImageRenderer + DocumentViewer + useImageDocument\n  tests) is sufficient.\n\nDrift reconciled: `ImageRenderer.test.tsx` drift-guard assertion updated\nfrom the slice-5-era 0.25 threshold to the current 1.0 threshold (raised\non main 2026-05-13).\n\n410 jest pass (was 381 on main, +29 from image tests) · 4/4 viewer e2e ·\n`tsc`, `eslint`, build clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2fca126c74bb8e3d18f92c515c2b45c2c6019756","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chriskonopka/consuming-app/git/trees/2fca126c74bb8e3d18f92c515c2b45c2c6019756"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chriskonopka/consuming-app/git/commits/b4cb5432f336239c6ac3b8747d32d8d0032c7887","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4922472?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chrisgoddard"