0e9","node_id":"C_kwDOSW_WwdoAKGJlZTcyMjk5MmMwYjZmYzhiMDViNWUwMjk1MGVlNjg1MTAzYjMwZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/chriskonopka/consuming-app/commit/d0bfbcb81926f3282fc877bb5c160c23b1d56620","sha":"d0bfbcb81926f3282fc877bb5c160c23b1d56620","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chriskonopka/consuming-app/commits/d0bfbcb81926f3282fc877bb5c160c23b1d56620"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/chriskonopka/consuming-app/commit/1410da28087c8f12ebc6af3b4e46a6f5b8872d39","sha":"1410da28087c8f12ebc6af3b4e46a6f5b8872d39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chriskonopka/consuming-app/commits/1410da28087c8f12ebc6af3b4e46a6f5b8872d39"}],"sha":"bee722992c0b6fc8b05b5e02950ee685103b30e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chriskonopka/consuming-app/commits/bee722992c0b6fc8b05b5e02950ee685103b30e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4922472?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chrisgoddard","id":4922472,"login":"chrisgoddard","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MjI0NzI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chriskonopka/consuming-app/commits/1410da28087c8f12ebc6af3b4e46a6f5b8872d39/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T18:21:37Z","email":"chris@Christophers-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Christopher Konopka"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T18:21:37Z","email":"chris@Christophers-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Christopher Konopka"},"message":"chore(viewer): raise drift-guard threshold from 25% to 50% of page height\n\nThe API''s citation builder consistently emits rectangles spanning whole\ncontent blocks rather than tight snippet bounds (h ≈ 26–48% of page\nheight for typical paragraph citations). At the original 25% threshold\nthe drift guard was rejecting most real citations as if they were\nmisaligned coordinates, surfacing \"Couldn''t locate this quote on the\npage.\" for the majority of citation clicks.\n\nRaise `DRIFT_GUARD_MAX_PAGE_FRACTION` to 0.50 so section-sized rectangles\nrender while the genuinely broken \"whole page\" case (>50%, e.g. h ≈ 88%\nor 92%) still rejects with the existing banner. Tracked back to the\nserver-side citation extraction as the root cause; this is the\ntactical fix while the API team tightens citation bounds.\n\nUpdates affected references: `REQUIREMENTS.md` §§5.2 / 5.6 / 6.6,\n`viewer/README.md`, the `CitationMarker` header comment, and the\nHighlightOverlay boundary tests (now exercising both the new 50%\nthreshold and a 25-50% rectangle that previously rejected).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bdef486642256ef2b39058eca9fe30009d8f39c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chriskonopka/consuming-app/git/trees/bdef486642256ef2b39058eca9fe30009d8f39c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chriskonopka/consuming-app/git/commits/1410da28087c8f12ebc6af3b4e46a6f5b8872d39","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4922472?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisgoddard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/