https://api.github.com/users/hodrigohamalho/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hodrigohamalho/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hodrigohamalho","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gateway-smashes/kuadrant-console/commits/43f39d00cdb83e509da8fd4795ebb64dc73d9778/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T16:56:05Z","email":"hodrigohamalho@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Ramalho"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T16:56:05Z","email":"hodrigohamalho@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Ramalho"},"message":"fix(hooks): always run the initial poll on mount, even in a hidden tab (fixes #15)\n\nusePollingEffect early-returned before the initial runOnce() when the tab was\nhidden at mount, so it skipped the one-shot fetch as well as the recurring\ninterval. Consumers flip their `loaded` flag inside the poll callback, so in\nany non-foreground tab (background, secondary, restored session) `loaded` never\nbecame true and the view sat on an infinite spinner / \"Loading metrics…\", its\nempty-state unreachable. Affected Cost, HTTPRoute Traffic Summary, and every\npolicy-detail Runtime Metrics section, among others.\n\nAlways fire one initial runOnce() on mount; gate only the recurring setInterval\non visibility. The visibilitychange listener still pauses/resumes the interval,\nand the cleanup is now registered on every path.\n\ntsc --noEmit and eslint clean.","tree":{"sha":"2cccba2e7bb7ef85c4df806e83e52d62ed197b7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gateway-smashes/kuadrant-console/git/trees/2cccba2e7bb7ef85c4df806e83e52d62ed197b7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gateway-smashes/kuadrant-console/git/commits/43f39d00cdb83e509da8fd4795ebb64dc73d9778","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252998?v=4","events_url":"https://api.gith