s child to parent.\nDrawing them that way aimed every arrow back up at razor-root-pom, which reads\nbackwards: the tree is understood from the root downward. Flipped at render time\nonly, so the detail panels keep the declared direction.\n\nThe hide-common-libs filter no longer counts parent edges. Inheriting from\nrazor-root-pom is not using a library, and counting it hid the three POMs at the\ntop of the tree by default at N=20.","tree":{"sha":"fb8725450a56bf6cd610a8f783282a1bcaab7a71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dfryer-r7/service-map-js/git/trees/fb8725450a56bf6cd610a8f783282a1bcaab7a71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dfryer-r7/service-map-js/git/commits/13e9dfc3a34f0e149207dc5757d367e7b5ad8205","verification":{"payload":"tree fb8725450a56bf6cd610a8f783282a1bcaab7a71\nparent f3ac8735aeb018ce99555f42cfddfa4bb8ddd628\nauthor David Fryer <david_fryer@rapid7.com> 1790866195 -0400\ncommitter David Fryer <david_fryer@rapid7.com> 1790866407 -0400\n\nPoint parent-POM arrows from parent to child\n\nA pom declares its parent, so the data stores those edges child to parent.\nDrawing them that way aimed every arrow back up at razor-root-pom, which reads\nbackwards: the tree is understood from the root downward. Flipped at render time\nonly, so the detail panels keep the declared direction.\n\nThe hide-common-libs filter no longer counts parent edges. Inheriting from\nrazor-root-pom is not using a library, and counting it hid the three POMs at the\ntop of the tree by default at N=20.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQQqaQ2nigJZiHnIecKLooyKOIXebAUCar5z5xsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQi6KMijiF3myEXwD/SgeR87KjUwJ+70XjEFt/\nQkCXoGcyG+naHMWKoxZ3xRcBAJMfd7QSE/j7x4afdqUt9B5yMCFdkX+yJypHxABp\n1LEP\n=zu7M\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T15:04:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/243605924?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dfryer-r7","id":243605924,"login":"dfryer-r7","node_id":"U_kgDODoUhpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dfryer-r7/service-map-js/commit/13e9dfc3a34f0e149207dc5757d367e7b5ad8205","node_id":"C_kwDOSYCPHdoAKDEzZTlkZmMzYTM0ZjBlMTQ5MjA3ZGM1NzU3ZDM2N2U3YjVhZDgyMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dfryer-r7/service-map-js/commit/f3ac8735aeb018ce99555f42cfddfa4bb8ddd628","sha":"f3ac8735aeb018ce99555f42cfddfa4bb8ddd628","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dfryer-r7/service-map-js/commits/f3ac8735aeb018ce99555f42cfddfa4bb8ddd628"}],"sha":"13e9dfc3a34f0e149207dc5757d367e7b5ad8205","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dfryer-r7/service-map-js/commits/13e9dfc3a34f0e149207dc5757d367e7b5ad8205"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/243605924?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dfryer-r7","id":243605924,"login":"dfryer-r7","node_id":"U_kgDODoUhpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dfryer-r7/service-map-js/commits/f3ac8735aeb018ce99555f42cfddfa4bb8ddd628/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:49:38Z","email":"david_fryer@rapid7.com","name":"David Fryer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:53:26Z","email":"david_fryer@rapid7.com","name":"David Fryer"},"message":"Rebuild the map from deployment registries instead of directory listings\n\nNode sets now come from the EC2 pipeline registry, the EKS Harness registry, the\nidr-frontend team roster and tf-razor-cambridge, so an archived repo left in the\nscan root can no longer appear as a live service. A backend node is a Maven\nmodule rather than a repo, which is what the domain monorepos needed: the five\nrazor-forensics modules are five nodes.\n\nHTTP edges come from client artifacts in each module''s pom, then validated by\nintersecting the consumer''s imports with the packages the provider declares. 349\nconfirmed, 12 dropped as stale declarations, 2 unverified and kept. Frontend to\nbackend edges resolve through fetchApi namespace, fetch-utils endpoint key, CPS\nhost mapping and route53, and are partial by nature: only repos on\n@rapid7/fetch-utils name a namespace at the call site.\n\nTwo parsing bugs fixed along the way. extractProjectInfo read the parent block''s\nartifactId and fell through to a dependency''s groupId. Datastore names stripped\ninterpolations before resolving locals, which is where \"master (MySQL)\" came\nfrom.\n\n220 service nodes / 521 edges, 340 dependency nodes / 2554 edges.","tree":{"sha":"24fd4dfdd9e1d7be279a36a0871002939cc5c569","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dfryer-r7/service-map-js/git/trees/24fd4dfdd9e1d7be279a36a0871002939cc5c569"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dfryer-r7/service-map-js/git/commits/f3ac8735aeb018ce99555f42cfddfa4bb8ddd628","verification":{"payload":"tree 24fd4dfdd9e1d7be279a36a0871002939cc5c569\nparent 6ff7573ad3cb6828c0068d90edd1b5b4c31ac6eb\nauthor David Fryer <david_fryer@rapid7.com> 1790866178 -0400\ncommitter David Fryer <david_fryer@rapid7.com> 1790866406 -0400\n\nRebuild the map from deployment registries instead of directory listings\n\nNode sets now come from the EC2 pipeline registry, the EKS Harness registry, the\nidr-frontend team roster and tf-razor-cambridge, so an archived repo left in the\nscan root can no longer appear as a live service. A backend node is a Maven\nmodule rather than a repo, which is what the domain monorepos needed: the five\nrazor-forensics modules are five nodes.\n\nHTTP edges come from client artifacts in each module''s pom, then validated by\nintersecting the consumer''s imports with the packages the provider declares. 349\nconfirmed, 12 dropped as stale declarations, 2 unverified and kept. Frontend to\nbackend edges resolve through fetchApi namespace, fetch-utils endpoint key, CPS\nhost mapping and route53, and are partial by nature: only repos on\n@rapid7/fetch-utils name a namespace at the call site.\n\nTwo parsing bugs fixed along the way. extractProjectInfo read the parent block''s\nartifactId and fell through to a dependency''s groupId. Datastore names stripped\ninterpolations before resolving locals, which is where \"master (MySQL)\" came\nfrom.\n\n220 service nodes / 521 edges, 340 dependency nodes / 2554 edges.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQQqaQ2nigJZiHnIecKLooyKOIXebAUCar5z5hsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQi6KMijiF3mzalwEA7eIAEudPf7KFxX8Cy0F2\nEdH/IzJVDfewyauYVVd9yF4A/ihvuaM6TFuvdgnSmnsAnPyXs8aH8C3rzhpHl8Se\n1h4L\n=IuXU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T15:04:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/243605924?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dfryer-r7","id":243605924,"login":"dfryer-r7","node_id":"U_kgDODoUhpA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dfryer-r7/service-map-js/commit/f3ac8735aeb018ce99555f42cfddfa4bb8ddd628","node_id":"C_kwDOSYCPHdoAKGYzYWM4NzM1YWViMDE4Y2U5OTU1NWY0MmNmZGRmYTRiYjhkZGQ2Mjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dfryer-r7/service-map-js/commit/6ff7573ad3cb6828c0068d90edd1b5b4c31ac6eb","sha":"6ff7573ad3cb6828c0068d90edd1b5b4c31ac6eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dfryer-r7/service-map-js/commits/6ff7573ad3cb6828c0068d90edd1b5b4c31ac6eb"}],"sha":"f3ac8735aeb018ce99555f42cfddfa4bb8ddd628","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dfryer-r7/service-map-js/commits/f3ac8735aeb018ce99555f42cfddfa4bb8ddd628"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/243605924?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfryer-r7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/u