ure DevOps / Jenkins. Distinct exit codes (0/2/3/4) so CI/CD can branch on the verdict.\n\nAll Python tests pass (8/8). CLI smoke-tested for all three exit paths.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"bc7c8eec7746bff7a72856b83dbbcb5593a2271e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/git/trees/bc7c8eec7746bff7a72856b83dbbcb5593a2271e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/git/commits/5f155bdb50e7466f04f7e2fbd906b74459141cf3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commit/5f155bdb50e7466f04f7e2fbd906b74459141cf3","node_id":"C_kwDOSYZgrNoAKDVmMTU1YmRiNTBlNzQ2NmYwNGY3ZTJmYmQ5MDZiNzQ0NTkxNDFjZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commit/cc7655c09972e957876a0221d9987d298a52ee20","sha":"cc7655c09972e957876a0221d9987d298a52ee20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/cc7655c09972e957876a0221d9987d298a52ee20"}],"sha":"5f155bdb50e7466f04f7e2fbd906b74459141cf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/5f155bdb50e7466f04f7e2fbd906b74459141cf3"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/cc7655c09972e957876a0221d9987d298a52ee20/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T06:29:00Z","email":"--get","name":"--get"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T06:29:00Z","email":"--get","name":"--get"},"message":"feat(api+ui): contract health score endpoint and editor badge (Epic 1.4)\n\nAdds GET /v1/contracts/{id}/health returning the weighted 7-dimension contract health score plus a Fluent UI tint badge next to the StatusBadge in the contract editor header. Context signals (label/approval/lineage/evidence) are stubbed pending Phase 2 persistence.\n\nBackend: 263/263 tests. Frontend: 26/26 tests + tsc clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"db0e98a47a8412720ef8188824a9cf2ee6fc7172","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/git/trees/db0e98a47a8412720ef8188824a9cf2ee6fc7172"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/git/commits/cc7655c09972e957876a0221d9987d298a52ee20","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commit/cc7655c09972e957876a0221d9987d298a52ee20","node_id":"C_kwDOSYZgrNoAKGNjNzY1NWMwOTk3MmU5NTc4NzZhMDIyMWQ5OTg3ZDI5OGE1MmVlMjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commit/f482e0d584483b43dae9bad3c4c16767bd3734bb","sha":"f482e0d584483b43dae9bad3c4c16767bd3734bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/f482e0d584483b43dae9bad3c4c16767bd3734bb"}],"sha":"cc7655c09972e957876a0221d9987d298a52ee20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/cc7655c09972e957876a0221d9987d298a52ee20"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/f482e0d584483b43dae9bad3c4c16767bd3734bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T06:06:51Z","email":"--get","name":"--get"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T06:06:51Z","email":"--get","name":"--get"},"message":"feat(engine): validate aiContext + add legal sample + frontend TS mirror\n\nCloses the immediate correctness/consistency gaps left by 17839a9:\n\n* OdcsContractValidator: add ValidateAiContext custom check covering\n  invalid EU AI Act tier, empty/missing useCase id, permittedUses vs\n  prohibitedUses overlap, and non-positive retentionForTraining.maxAgeDays.\n  Spec §16.1 rule 4: invalid contracts must not persist as active.\n* contracts/examples/legal-contract-extracts.contract.yaml: first sample\n  exercising the orqentisAiContext block end-to-end (Liability Summariser\n  RAG use case, EU/AU/US jurisdictions, high-risk tier).\n* frontend/src/models/AiContext.ts: TS mirror of AiContextExtension +\n  ContractHealthScore per copilot-instructions §4 (mirror backend DTO 1:1).\n* 6 new validator tests; 261/261 total pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"35c42ab8b28ba79edeeec52cf58352a4bfa1d510","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/git/trees/35c42ab8b28ba79edeeec52cf58352a4bfa1d510"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/git/commits/f482e0d584483b43dae9bad3c4c16767bd3734bb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commit/f482e0d584483b43dae9bad3c4c16767bd3734bb","node_id":"C_kwDOSYZgrNoAKGY0ODJlMGQ1ODQ0ODNiNDNkYWU5YmFkM2M0YzE2NzY3YmQzNzM0YmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commit/17839a9f6690c9c46ca1898ccea7de764a9aad50","sha":"17839a9f6690c9c46ca1898ccea7de764a9aad50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/17839a9f6690c9c46ca1898ccea7de764a9aad50"}],"sha":"f482e0d584483b43dae9bad3c4c16767bd3734bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/f482e0d584483b43dae9bad3c4c16767bd3734bb"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/17839a9f6690c9c46ca1898ccea7de764a9aad50/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T04:48:31Z","email":"--get","name":"--get"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T04:48:31Z","email":"--get","name":"--get"},"message":"feat(engine): ODCS aiContext extension + Contract Health Scorer (Phase 1 foundation)\n\nPhase 1 Epic 1.1 + 1.4 of the data-security-for-AI plan\n(see files/plan-data-security-for-ai.md).\n\n* Add AiContextExtension record with use cases, permitted/prohibited\n  uses, agents, and training retention policy. Persisted in ODCS\n  customProperties[] as ''orqentisAiContext'' so the v3.1.0 JSON Schema\n  stays untouched (spec §16.1 rule 4).\n* Wire AiContext through OdcsDocumentMapper parse + serialize paths.\n* Add IContractHealthScorer + ContractHealthScorer that produces a\n  0-100 score from seven weighted governance signals (schema validity,\n  quality pass-rate, freshness SLA, sensitivity label presence,\n  approval state, lineage completeness, evidence-cited ratio).\n  Borrowed from Collibra Trust Score pattern.\n* Register scorer in EngineServiceCollectionExtensions.\n* 12 new unit tests; 255/255 total pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3a5c2a3b981b6dedeff760297ed50002f4548165","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/git/trees/3a5c2a3b981b6dedeff760297ed50002f4548165"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/git/commits/17839a9f6690c9c46ca1898ccea7de764a9aad50","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commit/17839a9f6690c9c46ca1898ccea7de764a9aad50","node_id":"C_kwDOSYZgrNoAKDE3ODM5YTlmNjY5MGM5YzQ2Y2ExODk4Y2NlYTdkZTc2NGE5YWFkNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commit/696eb4bd1dd62e6c44345cce8cf3fa52be8c4e20","sha":"696eb4bd1dd62e6c44345cce8cf3fa52be8c4e20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/696eb4bd1dd62e6c44345cce8cf3fa52be8c4e20"}],"sha":"17839a9f6690c9c46ca1898ccea7de764a9aad50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/17839a9f6690c9c46ca1898ccea7de764a9aad50"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/696eb4bd1dd62e6c44345cce8cf3fa52be8c4e20/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T20:59:07Z","email":"--get","name":"--get"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T20:59:07Z","email":"--get","name":"--get"},"message":"fix(ui): apply designer review fixes (tint badges, subtle toolbar, tighter chrome)\n\nImplements P1 quick wins from the 2026-05-18 designer review:\n\n- StatusBadge: filled -> tint so ''Warned'' rows no longer scream amber across the report list (StatusBadge.tsx)\n\n- createSaveAction: removed appearance=''primary'' so the Save toolbar button is subtle like native Fabric editors (Notebook, Pipeline, Semantic Model)\n\n- ItemEditor: title uses Title3 (semantic h2) instead of a raw div with hero font tokens; replaced hand-rolled span divider with Fluent ToolbarDivider\n\n- AppShell: hostedRoot overflow auto -> hidden (prevents stray iframe scrollbars); background uses colorNeutralBackground2 closer to Fabric canvas\n\n- FabricPickers: replaced hardcoded fontSize: 11 / opacity: 0.6 / fontWeight: 600 / marginLeft: 8 with Fluent tokens\n\n- PolicyEditorPage: tightened root padding (XXL -> L/XL), Title2 -> Title3, footer divider added above Next/Cancel actions\n\n- EnforcementRunPage: same padding + Title3 tightening\n\nFull designer report: files/ui-designer-review-2026-05-18.md\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"989001d2267ed16839f63f3568f200d03ab9addd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/git/trees/989001d2267ed16839f63f3568f200d03ab9addd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/git/commits/696eb4bd1dd62e6c44345cce8cf3fa52be8c4e20","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commit/696eb4bd1dd62e6c44345cce8cf3fa52be8c4e20","node_id":"C_kwDOSYZgrNoAKDY5NmViNGJkMWRkNjJlNmM0NDM0NWNjZThjZjNmYTUyYmU4YzRlMjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commit/919edd643154507871142808c576ab599ba868d4","sha":"919edd643154507871142808c576ab599ba868d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/919edd643154507871142808c576ab599ba868d4"}],"sha":"696eb4bd1dd62e6c44345cce8cf3fa52be8c4e20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/696eb4bd1dd62e6c44345cce8cf3fa52be8c4e20"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/919edd643154507871142808c576ab599ba868d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T20:09:34Z","email":"--get","name":"--get"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T20:09:34Z","email":"--get","name":"--get"},"message":"fix(ui): remove duplicate workload sidebar; tighten item editor chrome\n\nInside the Fabric host iframe the workload now skips its internal NavShell sidebar. Fabric already provides the left rail, workspace switcher, and item tab bar; the workload MUST NOT render its own top-level navigation (App.tsx comment). Standalone (?__standalone=1) mode still gets NavShell.\n\nAlso tightens the ItemEditor header (smaller title, monospace truncated subtitle, single inline toolbar row), removes redundant Step N of 4 + breadcrumb in the Policy wizard, ensures subtitle Caption1 is block in Report/Policy/Editor, and softens the Fabric items picker error to an info-level message guiding users to paste the OneLake path.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"720ebe6f74d0f027f1a5e2a410fc210693defb6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/git/trees/720ebe6f74d0f027f1a5e2a410fc210693defb6c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/git/commits/919edd643154507871142808c576ab599ba868d4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commit/919edd643154507871142808c576ab599ba868d4","node_id":"C_kwDOSYZgrNoAKDkxOWVkZDY0MzE1NDUwNzg3MTE0MjgwOGM1NzZhYjU5OWJhODY4ZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commit/9d813a0220c72a28f83d40893712e572881f75cd","sha":"9d813a0220c72a28f83d40893712e572881f75cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/9d813a0220c72a28f83d40893712e572881f75cd"}],"sha":"919edd643154507871142808c576ab599ba868d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/919edd643154507871142808c576ab599ba868d4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/9d813a0220c72a28f83d40893712e572881f75cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T12:50:08Z","email":"--get","name":"--get"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T12:50:08Z","email":"--get","name":"--get"},"message":"fix(ui): wire workspaceId via Fabric SDK and route fabric clients to /v1/fabric\n\nThe Contract/Policy/Report item editors were failing with 400 (missing\nX-Workspace-Id) because Fabric does not pass workspaceId on the iframe URL.\nResolve workspaceId via client.itemCrud.getItem(itemId) when not present\nin the bootstrap path. With that, /v1/contracts, /v1/activator/rules and\n/v1/reports/audit all return 200.\n\nAlso fix /v1/ops/workspaces (does not exist on backend) → /v1/workspaces,\nand /v1/ops/workspaces/<id>/fabric-items / /v1/ops/lakehouses/<id>/tables\n(do not exist) → /v1/fabric/<wsid>/... matching FabricProxyController.\n\nSurface silent token-acquisition failures via console.error in\nuseFabricSdk so future auth issues are visible in the iframe console.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a7ae1e6e49abe38a59208d02405705dfa96adde9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/git/trees/a7ae1e6e49abe38a59208d02405705dfa96adde9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/git/commits/9d813a0220c72a28f83d40893712e572881f75cd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commit/9d813a0220c72a28f83d40893712e572881f75cd","node_id":"C_kwDOSYZgrNoAKDlkODEzYTAyMjBjNzJhMjhmODNkNDA4OTM3MTJlNTcyODgxZjc1Y2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commit/ff0453a8f4b5c5fca0455cf811044b1efe768a3b","sha":"ff0453a8f4b5c5fca0455cf811044b1efe768a3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/ff0453a8f4b5c5fca0455cf811044b1efe768a3b"}],"sha":"9d813a0220c72a28f83d40893712e572881f75cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/9d813a0220c72a28f83d40893712e572881f75cd"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/ff0453a8f4b5c5fca0455cf811044b1efe768a3b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T12:11:57Z","email":"--get","name":"--get"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T12:11:57Z","email":"--get","name":"--get"},"message":"fix(ui): stop infinite setCorrelationId loop crashing item editors\n\nEach call to useFabricSdk() previously generated its own local correlationId\nvia useState and unconditionally pushed it into the Zustand store inside an\neffect when it differed from the store value. Two sibling consumers\n(AppShell for theme + per-route RouteErrorBoundary wrapper in App.tsx) each\nseeded a different id and then ping-ponged setState forever, hitting React\nerror #185 (Maximum update depth exceeded). The whole workload UI crashed\nwhen any Contract / Policy / Report item was opened in Fabric.\n\nUse a module-level singleton getProcessCorrelationId() so every hook\ninstance reads the same value, and only seed the store once when it is\nstill null. Also adds debugging affordances (FRAME_EVAL, FRAME_TEXT, LOG)\nto the Playwright controller used to capture the original stack trace\nthrough the cross-origin Fabric iframe.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0d69fd156f8509beb25231c19045674bd3aebb5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/git/trees/0d69fd156f8509beb25231c19045674bd3aebb5c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/git/commits/ff0453a8f4b5c5fca0455cf811044b1efe768a3b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commit/ff0453a8f4b5c5fca0455cf811044b1efe768a3b","node_id":"C_kwDOSYZgrNoAKGZmMDQ1M2E4ZjRiNWM1ZmNhMDQ1NWNmODExMDQ0YjFlZmU3NjhhM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commit/76250b5738d53bb7051ae209a847ef84076549fa","sha":"76250b5738d53bb7051ae209a847ef84076549fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/76250b5738d53bb7051ae209a847ef84076549fa"}],"sha":"ff0453a8f4b5c5fca0455cf811044b1efe768a3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/ff0453a8f4b5c5fca0455cf811044b1efe768a3b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mjtpena/fabric-contract-intelligence/commits/76250b5738d53bb7051ae209a847ef84076549fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-16T23:19:06Z","email":"--get","name":"--get"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T23:19:06Z","email":"--get","name":"--get"},"message":"